  {
   "id": 12,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "CHARACTER MOTION\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 2, CC 33 to 48\n   1 Character path\n   2 Character speed\n   3 Toward the lens\n   4 Who moves\n   5 Body in frame\n   6 The camera's attitude\n   7 Speed within a move\n   8 Drawn on ones, twos or threes\n   9 Overshoot\n  10 Overlap\n  11 Path shape\n  12 Squash and stretch\n  13 Key poses per line\n  14 Mouth shapes\n  15 Animation feel\n  16 Poses and body control\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 2, CC 49 to 64\n   1 Movement rules\n   2 Acting moves\n   3 Face acting\n   4 Walking back and forth\n   5 Making an entrance\n   6 Walking out\n   7 Squaring off\n   8 Standing up and sitting down\n   9 suite: Crossing\n  10 suite: Snappy cartoon moves\n  11 suite: Grounded realism (how they move)\n  12 suite: The chase\n  13 suite: Bursting in\n  14 suite: Rubbery cartoon bodies\n  15 suite: Heavy and real (weight and landing)\n  16 suite: Poker face\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 2, CC 65 to 80\n   1 suite: 1930s rubber-hose cartoon\n   2 suite: Budget TV animation\n   3 suite: The standoff\n   4 suite: Storming out\n   5 suite: Grand arrival\n   6 pair: When a person approaches, the camera pushes in\n   7 pair: When a character approaches, personal space shrinks\n   8 pair: When characters speed up, the cutting speeds up\n   9 pair: When the wind-up grows, the move lands bigger\n  10 pair: When the face goes big, the body follows\n  11 pair: When the eyes dart, the expression changes next\n  12 pair: When a character walks toward the lens, the shot becomes a close-up\n  13 pair: When a hand reaches toward the lens, it looms huge\n  14 pair: When the listener moves and the speaker stays still, the edit turns to the listener\n  15 pair: When a move snaps into place, it bounces past its mark\n  16 pair: When moves bounce past their mark, the scene feels playful\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 2, CC 81 to 96\n   1 pair: When a character stops suddenly, the hair and clothes keep going\n   2 pair: When a character moves fast, every frame gets its own drawing\n   3 pair: When moves travel in straight lines, the character looks robotic\n   4 pair: When they pace, they start talking to themselves\n   5 pair: When the pacing speeds up, the cuts come faster\n   6 pair: When the entrance is big, the talking stops\n   7 pair: When the door is slammed, silence follows\n   8 pair: When we stay with the one left behind, loneliness grows\n   9 pair: When the shot holds after they go, it stays too long on purpose\n  10 pair: When they square off, tension climbs\n  11 pair: When they square off, the camera circles them\n  12 pair: When they shoot to their feet, the speaker holds the power\n  13 pair: When the room goes quiet, the standoff holds longer\n  14 pair: When a stranger first appears as a shadow, trust drops\n  15 pairs: Movement drives the cutting\n  16 pairs: Acting from the inside out\nCV-CC 5: MIDI channel 2, CC 97 to 100\n   1 pairs: Coming at the lens\n   2 pairs: Cartoon physics\n   3 pairs: Smooth or stiff\n   4 pairs: The fight ends at the door"
   },
