   "data": {
    "text": "MOVEMENT WITH LINES\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 4, CC 81 to 96\n   1 Size of gesture\n   2 How still this person is\n   3 Blink\n   4 Anticipation\n   5 Leads the move\n   6 Facial expression\n   7 Eye darts\n   8 Posture\n   9 Touch\n  10 Walk and talk\n  11 Business with a prop\n  12 Move on the line\n  13 The listener's body\n  14 Saying it with their back turned\n  15 A habit of their own\n  16 Copying each other's body\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 4, CC 97 to 112\n   1 Answering without words\n   2 Talking side by side\n   3 The body says the opposite\n   4 Talking through a door\n   5 suite: The walk and talk\n   6 suite: Busy hands\n   7 suite: The task falls apart\n   8 suite: Freeze on the line\n   9 suite: The real reaction\n  10 suite: Thinking face\n  11 suite: Stage-size acting\n  12 suite: Falling in step\n  13 suite: Bundle of nerves\n  14 suite: The confession in the car\n  15 suite: The locked bathroom\n  16 pair: When a big line lands, the body freezes\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 5, CC 1 to 16\n   1 pair: When the speaker gets closer to the truth, the listener leans in\n   2 pair: When the anger rises, the task gets rougher\n   3 pair: When the task falls apart, a laugh comes\n   4 pair: When they walk and talk, the shots get longer\n   5 pair: When the wind-up is big, the body stretches far on the release\n   6 pair: When the eyes keep darting, the character reads as nervous\n   7 pair: When the eyes snap to something, the eyes lead the turn\n   8 pair: When a character stops blinking, they become unsettling\n   9 pair: When a touch is held, the beat turns tender\n  10 pair: When they turn their back to hide tears, the feeling stays hidden\n  11 pair: When they turn their back, the eyes stop meeting\n  12 pair: When the habit comes from lying, the gap between words and meaning grows\n  13 pair: When someone copies the habit, the two start mirroring\n  14 pair: When two people mirror each other, warmth grows between them\n  15 pair: When two people mirror each other, they stand closer\n  16 pair: When the asker pushes for words, they square off\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 5, CC 17 to 28\n   1 pair: When they sit side by side, more gets said\n   2 pair: When the body says the opposite, said and meant pull apart\n   3 pair: When both touch the door, tenderness comes through it\n   4 pair: When the barrier is more solid, loneliness grows\n   5 pair: When the take runs long, the acting loosens up\n   6 pair: When they walk and talk through the night, they open up\n   7 pair: When everyone stays very still, the smallest reaction says everything\n   8 pairs: The body moves with the words\n   9 pairs: Comic business\n  10 pairs: The eyes give it away\n  11 pairs: Growing close\n  12 pairs: Doors and last words"
