   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "WARDROBE\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 12, CC 33 to 48\n   1 Main: era of the clothes\n   2 Main: cheap to expensive\n   3 Main: how much skin is covered\n   4 Main: looks or function\n   5 Main: the job the clothes do\n   6 Main: wear and tear\n   7 Fit\n   8 Casual to formal\n   9 Clothes against the set\n  10 Crowd: era of the clothes\n  11 Crowd: cheap to expensive\n  12 Crowd: how much skin is covered\n  13 Crowd: looks or function\n  14 Crowd: the job the clothes do\n  15 Crowd: wear and tear\n  16 All different to all alike\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 12, CC 49 to 64\n   1 True to the time\n   2 Background against the main character\n   3 A change of clothes marks the turn\n   4 The group dresses as one\n   5 The one piece that clashes\n   6 Clothes that are not theirs\n   7 Taking off the uniform\n   8 suite: Main character's clothes lens\n   9 suite: Background clothes lens\n  10 suite: Period truth\n  11 suite: Deliberate anachronism\n  12 suite: Working uniform\n  13 suite: Dressed to impress\n  14 suite: Falling apart\n  15 suite: Frontier\n  16 suite: The gang look\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 12, CC 65 to 80\n   1 suite: Growing into it\n   2 suite: Laying down the badge\n   3 pair: A new outfit marks a change in the character\n   4 pair: A disguise is followed by its unmasking\n   5 pair: Clashing clothes get noticed\n   6 pair: When the crowd is in rags, the hero's clean clothes make them the only one\n   7 pair: When the hero is the only one dressed that way, the eye finds them in the crowd\n   8 pair: When the hero dresses unlike everyone else, they feel out of place\n   9 pair: When the hero's clothes are luxury, they stand out from the room\n  10 pair: When the clothes are very formal, people move stiffly\n  11 pair: When the clothes are baggy, a trip or a snag is waiting\n  12 pair: When a layer of clothing comes off, the characters get closer\n  13 pair: When the hero suits up in armor, big action follows\n  14 pair: When the outfit is only for show, the hero is wrong for the job\n  15 pair: When the crowd dresses in 1920s clothes, the room follows\n  16 pair: When the background clothes are clearly wrong for the time, the scene turns into a joke\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 12, CC 81 to 96\n   1 pair: When everyone wears the same uniform, the place feels oppressive\n   2 pair: When the crowd's clothes are torn and dirty, the place reads as run down\n   3 pair: When the crowd is bundled up, the picture turns cool\n   4 pair: When the crowd wears work clothes, the place reads as a working site\n   5 pair: When the crowd dresses only for show, the room is rich\n   6 pair: When the change of clothes is bigger, the inner change shows\n   7 pair: When everyone stares at the new look, pride rises\n   8 pair: When the hero breaks from the group's look, they stand apart\n   9 pair: When the group's look splits in two, so do the sides\n  10 pair: When the piece clashes more, the eye goes there first\n  11 pair: When the odd piece is a memory of someone, nostalgia comes\n  12 pair: When the clothes fit worse, we feel for them\n  13 pair: When they are teased for the bad fit, shame rises\n  14 pair: When the clothes finally fit, the change shows\n  15 pair: When the uniform is folded and left behind, there is no going back\n  16 pair: When taking off the uniform matters more, the look turns\nCV-CC 5: MIDI channel 12, CC 97 to 101\n   1 pair: When the uniform comes off in front of someone they trust, tenderness grows\n   2 pairs: Clothes tell the story\n   3 pairs: The standout hero\n   4 pairs: Dressed wrong for it\n   5 pairs: The change you can wear"
   },
