   "id": 136,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "COMEDY\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 2, CC 49 to 64\n   1 Kind of joke\n   2 What the joke is about\n   3 Pause before the punchline\n   4 Escalation\n   5 Absurdity\n   6 Deadpan to broad\n   7 Cringe\n   8 Setup and payoff\n   9 Scenes from setup to payoff\n  10 Laughs per minute\n  11 Who carries the joke\n  12 Reaction to the joke\n  13 Running gag\n  14 Callback\n  15 Rule of three\n  16 Physical comedy\nCV-CC 2: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 2, CC 65 to 80\n   1 Wordplay\n   2 Misdirection\n   3 Irony\n   4 Understatement\n   5 Out of place in a strange world\n   6 Visual gag\n   7 Subversion\n   8 Comic edit\n   9 Comic sound\n  10 Comic flaw\n  11 Comic premise\n  12 The topper\n  13 Oddly specific\n  14 Talking to the camera\n  15 Exaggeration\n  16 Humiliation\nCV-CC 3: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 2, CC 81 to 96\n   1 The lie that grows\n   2 Misunderstanding\n   3 Cutaway gag\n   4 Serious answer to a silly question\n   5 Catchphrase\n   6 The button\n   7 Tiny want, huge effort\n   8 Insults and roasts\n   9 Parody\n  10 Satire\n  11 Joke about the film itself\n  12 The joke that falls flat\n  13 Seeing the gag coming\n  14 Made up on the spot\n  15 Cartoon rules\n  16 The turn from funny to sad\nCV-CC 4: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 2, CC 97 to 112\n   1 Making fun of yourself\n   2 The bad disguise\n   3 The tag scene\n   4 Talking past the point\n   5 Saying it back\n   6 Cracking up\n   7 The wrong person overhears\n   8 Trying too hard to be cool\n   9 Taking it literally\n  10 The plan that fails at step one\n  11 The long walk of shame\n  12 The deliberately cheap effect\n  13 The joke you catch the second time\n  14 Keeping up polite appearances\n  15 The one who never gets the joke\n  16 The joke we only hear\nCV-CC 5: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 3, CC 1 to 16\n   1 Interrupted at the worst moment\n   2 Mistaken for someone else\n   3 The animal that steals the scene\n   4 The fumbled hello\n   5 suite: Comedy lens\n   6 suite: Where the laugh comes from\n   7 suite: Deadpan\n   8 suite: Slapstick\n   9 suite: Mockumentary\n  10 suite: Screwball\n  11 suite: Cringe comedy\n  12 suite: Absurdist\n  13 suite: Dark comedy\n  14 suite: Rom-com banter\n  15 suite: Snowball disaster\n  16 suite: Pull-back reveal\nCV-CC 6: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 3, CC 17 to 32\n   1 suite: Smash cut contradiction\n   2 suite: Background gags\n   3 suite: Farce\n   4 suite: Topping the joke, twice\n   5 suite: Punching up\n   6 suite: The aside\n   7 suite: Oddly specific world\n   8 suite: Blind to their flaw\n   9 suite: The cutaway that contradicts\n  10 suite: Bigger than life\n  11 suite: Slow-burn gags\n  12 suite: Stranger in a strange land\n  13 suite: Twisting the familiar\n  14 suite: Spoof movie\n  15 suite: Roast battle\n  16 suite: The flop\nCV-CC 7: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 3, CC 33 to 48\n   1 suite: Loose and improvised\n   2 suite: Sad clown\n   3 suite: Sharp satire\n   4 suite: Sitcom habits\n   5 suite: Petty quest\n   6 suite: Heard through the wall\n   7 suite: Dinner with the in-laws\n   8 suite: The cool act collapses\n   9 suite: Best laid plans\n  10 suite: Cardboard and string\n  11 suite: One for the second watch\n  12 suite: The proposal that keeps failing\n  13 suite: The crash in the next room\n  14 suite: Always a beat behind\n  15 suite: Silent-film physical comedy\n  16 suite: Mockumentary (full style)\nCV-CC 8: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 3, CC 49 to 64\n   1 suite: Genre spoof, gag after gag\n   2 suite: Absurd sketch logic\n   3 suite: Fast visual comedy cut to the beat\n   4 suite: Dark comedy of bad plans\n   5 suite: Sweet clown with a broken heart\n   6 suite: Deadpan stillness and long pauses\n   7 suite: Rapid wordplay and wit\n   8 suite: Squirm comedy of the clueless boss\n   9 suite: Gag every second, played straight\n  10 pair: When a joke's setup is planted, the payoff lands\n  11 pair: When the escalation rises, the absurdity rises\n  12 pair: When the pause before the punchline grows, laughs per minute drop but each lands harder\n  13 pair: After a big joke, cut to a reaction\n  14 pair: Two of a pattern, then the break\n  15 pair: \"I'll never\", then they do\n  16 pair: After a cringe, a pointed silence\nCV-CC 9: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 3, CC 65 to 80\n   1 pair: As trouble escalates, the frame widens\n   2 pair: A running gag returns, bigger\n   3 pair: A joke line returns in a tender moment\n   4 pair: Something absurd, nobody reacts\n   5 pair: Misdirection pays off with a pull-back\n   6 pair: After tension, a laugh breaks it\n   7 pair: When a joke lands, a topper follows\n   8 pair: When a lie wobbles, a bigger lie covers it\n   9 pair: When the lie collapses, someone is humiliated\n  10 pair: When a misunderstanding deepens, the chaos grows\n  11 pair: When someone is humiliated in front of others, the cringe rises\n  12 pair: When a blind flaw grows, the character is set back\n  13 pair: When a character talks to us, the others react a beat late\n  14 pair: An oddly specific detail comes back later\n  15 pair: When the physical comedy turns destructive, things shatter\n  16 pair: When the joke is built on a misunderstanding, the confusion keeps getting deeper\nCV-CC 10: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 3, CC 81 to 96\n   1 pair: When the joke aims at the powerful, the audience laughs harder\n   2 pair: When the comedy goes cartoon-big, the falls get bigger\n   3 pair: When the payoff comes long after its setup, the laugh is bigger\n   4 pair: When the joke rests on the straight one, they stay perfectly calm\n   5 pair: When someone lands a sharp comeback, the pecking order wobbles\n   6 pair: When a disaster is treated as no big deal, the laugh comes in the pause\n   7 pair: When someone is badly out of place, the awkward moments pile up\n   8 pair: When more sight gags fill the frame, the laughs come faster\n   9 pair: When the setup feels very familiar, the payoff gets turned upside down\n  10 pair: When the comic idea is crystal clear, the scene can push it further and further\n  11 pair: When the situation keeps escalating, everything gets exaggerated\n  12 pair: When things get exaggerated far enough, they tip into the absurd\n  13 pair: When a cutaway shows the opposite of what was just said, the laugh lands on the cut\n  14 pair: When a silly question gets a dead serious answer, the reactions grow\n  15 pair: When a silly answer turns into a lecture, someone says it back\n  16 pair: When everyone waits for the catchphrase, holding it back gets the laugh\nCV-CC 11: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 3, CC 97 to 112\n   1 pair: When the catchphrase comes back with a new meaning, the callback turns sweet\n   2 pair: When the topper lands, a button closes the scene\n   3 pair: When the button lands, the scene ends on it\n   4 pair: When a tiny want meets a huge effort, the trouble escalates\n   5 pair: When the tiny want is won and ruined, someone is humiliated\n   6 pair: When a roast stings, a better comeback follows\n   7 pair: When a roast is loving, the warmth between them grows\n   8 pair: When a roast goes too far, everything stops\n   9 pair: When a parody copies shot for shot, the twist gets the laugh\n  10 pair: When the satire bites harder, the jokes get darker\n  11 pair: When the film jokes about itself, a character talks to us\n  12 pair: When a joke falls flat, the silence stretches\n  13 pair: When the teller explains the failed joke, they talk past the point\n  14 pair: When we see the gag coming, the payoff gets a bigger laugh\n  15 pair: When the trap is shown clearly, the fall comes\n  16 pair: When the scene loosens up, the lines start to overlap\nCV-CC 12: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 4, CC 1 to 16\n   1 pair: When the scene feels improvised, someone cracks up\n   2 pair: When cartoon rules take over, the falls stop hurting\n   3 pair: When a joke turns sad on one line, the music drops away\n   4 pair: When tears turn into a laugh, the release comes through laughing\n   5 pair: When self-mockery hides hurt, mixed feelings show\n   6 pair: When the disguise slips, the lie grows bigger\n   7 pair: When a tag scene ties back, an old joke returns\n   8 pair: When someone talks past the point, the cringe rises\n   9 pair: When something absurd is said, someone says it back\n  10 pair: When the performers laugh out loud, the warmth grows\n  11 pair: When the wrong person overhears more, the mix-up grows\n  12 pair: When the one who overheard tells everyone, more of the room is in on it\n  13 pair: When the speaker turns around and sees who heard, the cringe rises\n  14 pair: When the cool act collapses completely, someone is humiliated\n  15 pair: When someone tries harder to be cool, they start copying the cool one\n  16 pair: When the humiliation is bigger, the walk out gets longer\nCV-CC 13: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 4, CC 17 to 32\n   1 pair: When the walk of shame gets longer, shame gets heavier\n   2 pair: When one person claps during the walk out, the cringe rises\n   3 pair: When the words are acted out in full, the slapstick gets bigger\n   4 pair: When the literal one is new to the language, they feel out of place\n   5 pair: When the careful plan fails at once, things get worse\n   6 pair: When every failed plan brings a longer one, it becomes a running gag\n   7 pair: When they make it up and make it worse, everyone jumps in to fix it\n   8 pair: When the effect looks cheaper, the absurdity grows\n   9 pair: When the cheap effect copies an old style in full, the parody shows\n  10 pair: When the joke is hidden deeper, the payoff comes from further away\n  11 pair: When they stay more polite, what they mean slips under the words\n  12 pair: When everyone's manners crack at the end, the room stops dead\n  13 pair: When one person never gets the joke, they stop fitting the group\n  14 pair: When the one who never got it makes the best joke, it tops them all\n  15 pair: When the crash stays out of sight, the faces carry the joke\n  16 pair: When they walk back in calm after the crash, the understatement lands\nCV-CC 14: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 4, CC 33 to 48\n   1 pair: When the big moment keeps getting cut off, it becomes a running gag\n   2 pair: When the big moment is lost, the question stays open\n   3 pair: When they happily play the wrong person, the lie grows\n   4 pair: When the mix-up grows, the real one keeps nearly turning up\n   5 pair: When the real one turns up, every problem meets in one room\n   6 pair: When the animal steals more of the scene, the eye leaves the people\n   7 pair: When the humans pretend not to see the animal, the polite act strains\n   8 pair: When the greeting fumbles longer, the cringe rises\n   9 pair: When the greeting ends in bumped heads, the slapstick lands\n  10 pair: When the details are absurdly specific, the sadness underneath shows through\n  11 pair: When the talk speeds up, the chaos around them grows\n  12 pair: When the stunt is shown wide in one shot, our jaw drops\n  13 pair: When we see the trap before the hero does, the laugh grows\n  14 pair: When the face stays blank, the chaos around gets funnier\n  15 pair: When someone looks straight at the camera, the laugh doubles\n  16 pair: When the next shot shows the opposite of the interview, the irony is plain\nCV-CC 15: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 4, CC 49 to 64\n   1 pair: When the genre's rules are clearly borrowed, breaking them gets the laugh\n   2 pair: When the film jokes about being a film, the laughs come faster\n   3 pair: When nobody in the scene blinks at the absurd, it gets funnier\n   4 pair: When one silly idea is followed with strict logic, it climbs higher and higher\n   5 pair: When the joke aims at people in charge, the rules get sillier\n   6 pair: When a joke is quietly planted early, it pays off much later\n   7 pair: When one person cracks up, the laughing spreads around the room\n   8 pair: When greed blinds them, every fix makes it worse\n   9 pair: When the rich look down on the little hero, the gags punch upward\n  10 pair: When almost nothing is said, each line is held longer before the cut\n  11 pair: When a brilliant line lands, someone tops it\n  12 pair: When a phrase comes back with a new meaning, it hits harder than the first time\n  13 pair: When a dead joke gets explained, the silence grows\n  14 pair: When they need to be liked, they try too hard and it gets worse\n  15 pair: When the actors play it dead straight, the laughs get bigger\n  16 pair: When a phrase is taken word for word, the picture shows it\nCV-CC 16: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 4, CC 65 to 80\n   1 pair: When gags fill every corner of the frame, the laughs never stop\n   2 pairs: Joke machine\n   3 pairs: Long-game comedy\n   4 pairs: Comic reversals\n   5 pairs: The camera sells the joke\n   6 pairs: The farce engine\n   7 pairs: Stacking laughs\n   8 pairs: Comedy of a flaw\n   9 pairs: Smash and scatter\n  10 pairs: The cartoon spiral\n  11 pairs: The calm one cracks\n  12 pairs: The flop spiral\n  13 pairs: Petty quest to ruin\n  14 pairs: Roast night\n  15 pairs: Laugh, then cry\n  16 pairs: Sitcom scene shape\nCV-CC 17: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 4, CC 81 to 94\n   1 pairs: From one overheard line\n   2 pairs: From cool to the door\n   3 pairs: Plan to pandemonium\n   4 pairs: Silent-film physical comedy: the moves\n   5 pairs: Mockumentary: the moves\n   6 pairs: Genre spoof, gag after gag: the moves\n   7 pairs: Absurd sketch logic: the moves\n   8 pairs: Fast visual comedy cut to the beat: the moves\n   9 pairs: Dark comedy of bad plans: the moves\n  10 pairs: Sweet clown with a broken heart: the moves\n  11 pairs