   "data": {
    "text": "COMEDY FROM THE MIX\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 4, CC 97 to 112\n   1 How different the personalities are\n   2 Chaos in an orderly room\n   3 Gap in rank\n   4 What the mix does to the plot\n   5 What the mix does to the characters\n   6 Laughs from the mix\n   7 The double act\n   8 The straight man\n   9 Doesn't fit this group\n  10 Clash of egos\n  11 Who is in on it, around the room\n  12 Who sides with whom\n  13 The unwanted guest\n  14 Chemistry\n  15 Everything stops\n  16 Comic montage\nCV-CC 2: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 5, CC 1 to 16\n   1 The punching bag\n   2 Making something tiny epic\n   3 Chase played for laughs\n   4 The near miss\n   5 Funny music\n   6 The narrator joke\n   7 Everyone plays along\n   8 A war fought politely\n   9 Two talks that cross\n  10 Everyone fixing it at once\n  11 Shot like the wrong kind of film\n  12 Every problem in one room\n  13 Copying someone, badly\n  14 suite: Comedy from the mix lens\n  15 suite: Straight one and funny one\n  16 suite: Chaos agent\nCV-CC 3: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 5, CC 17 to 32\n   1 suite: The odd couple\n   2 suite: Calm in the madness\n   3 suite: Doesn't belong here\n   4 suite: The petty war\n   5 suite: Everyone knows but one\n   6 suite: Status swap\n   7 suite: The worst possible guest\n   8 suite: Banter\n   9 suite: Trickster stirs the pot\n  10 suite: Shifting loyalties\n  11 suite: Door-slamming farce\n  12 suite: Slapstick chase\n  13 suite: Wry narrator\n  14 suite: Dry double act\n  15 suite: The wrong man\n  16 suite: Sweet poison\nCV-CC 4: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 5, CC 33 to 48\n   1 suite: Too many hands\n   2 suite: A western in the living room\n   3 suite: Two tables, one conversation\n   4 suite: Rapid-fire screwball\n   5 suite: Romantic comedy meet-cute\n   6 suite: Loose improvised hangout comedy\n   7 suite: One wild night teen comedy\n   8 suite: Romantic comedy of manners\n   9 pair: When a chaos character enters an orderly room, the cringe rises\n  10 pair: When opposite personality types share the room, more of the laughs come from the mix\n  11 pair: When the gap in rank grows, the plot takes a turn\n  12 pair: Pride before a fall\n  13 pair: When the unwanted guest arrives, the room falls into chaos\n  14 pair: When the egos clash, the plot takes a detour\n  15 pair: When the one who doesn't know gets close to the secret, the cringe rises\n  16 pair: When the chaos grows, the straight man's calm sells the laugh\nCV-CC 5: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 5, CC 49 to 64\n   1 pair: When the odd one out tries harder, the group pulls away\n   2 pair: When the sides switch, the status flips\n   3 pair: When the chemistry grows, the characters change\n   4 pair: When the calm one finally loses it, the biggest laugh lands\n   5 pair: When a comic pair trades lines faster, the spark between them grows\n   6 pair: When the room stops dead, the record scratches\n   7 pair: When the room stops, the cringe rises\n   8 pair: When the comic montage starts, the cuts land on the beat\n   9 pair: When the montage shows failed attempts, the disaster escalates\n  10 pair: When the punching bag keeps losing, our sympathy grows\n  11 pair: When the punching bag finally wins big, the release floods in\n  12 pair: When something tiny is made epic, the picture slows down\n  13 pair: When the epic fuss cuts hard to reality, a smash cut pops it\n  14 pair: When a comic chase picks up, things crash\n  15 pair: When the near misses pile up, the room falls into chaos\n  16 pair: When two people miss each other by a second, the tension jumps\nCV-CC 6: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 5, CC 65 to 80\n   1 pair: When the funny music stops dead, the silence gets the laugh\n   2 pair: When the music copies every step, the physical comedy gets bigger\n   3 pair: When the narrator jumps in with an intro, the frame freezes\n   4 pair: When the voice-over says one thing and the picture shows another, the narrator joke lands\n   5 pair: When everyone plays along, the absurdity grows\n   6 pair: When the manners must hold, the fight goes polite\n   7 pair: When egos clash at a formal table, the war goes polite\n   8 pair: When the polite war turns into a real fight, chaos fills the room\n   9 pair: When the two talks cross more, misunderstandings grow\n  10 pair: When a crossed line gives away a secret, more people know it\n  11 pair: When more helpers make it worse, the trouble escalates\n  12 pair: When every helper breaks something new, chaos fills the room\n  13 pair: When the scene copies another kind of film more fully, it becomes a parody\n  14 pair: When the borrowed style snaps back to normal, a hard comic cut pops it\n  15 pair: When the lie keeps growing, every problem heads for one room\n  16 pair: When more problems meet in one room, the near misses pile up\nCV-CC 7: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 5, CC 81 to 96\n   1 pair: When the farce blows up into a chase, the comic chase begins\n   2 pair: When the copying goes further, the cringe rises\n   3 pair: When the copied one starts copying back, a double act is born\n   4 pair: When they talk over each other, the sparks between them grow\n   5 pair: When the calm one finally loses it, the biggest laugh lands\n   6 pair: When two strangers bump into each other, the spark starts\n   7 pair: When the talk wanders off topic, the friends feel more real\n   8 pair: When friends roast each other with love, the warmth between them grows\n   9 pair: When the little hero keeps losing, we root for them harder\n  10 pair: When the boss pretends to be one of the team, the room goes stiff\n  11 pair: When the careful friend is dragged along, the wild one pushes harder\n  12 pair: When polite words say the opposite of the wish, the spark grows\n  13 pairs: The mix makes it funny\n  14 pairs: The house party engine\n  15 pairs: The secret in the room\n  16 pairs: The pair that grows\nCV-CC 8: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 5, CC 97 to 106\n   1 pairs: Epic fuss, then popped\n   2 pairs: Chase to crash\n   3 pairs: Farce at the doors\n   4 pairs: Manners at war\n   5 pairs: From the wrong man to a farce\n   6 pairs: Rapid-fire screwball: the moves\n   7 pairs: Romantic comedy meet-cute: the moves\n   8 pairs: Loose improvised hangout comedy: the moves\n   9 pairs: One wild night teen comedy: the moves\n  10 pairs: Romantic comedy of manners: the moves"
