   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "MUSIC & SOUND\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 6, CC 1 to 16\n   1 Score (music only we hear)\n   2 Sound density\n   3 Sound against the cut\n   4 Music\n   5 No music\n   6 Sound effects around the scene\n   7 Music speeds up or slows down\n   8 Music turns sad or bright\n   9 The lead instrument\n  10 Style of music\n  11 Music crosses over\n  12 A character's own tune\n  13 Someone hums or sings\n  14 A song performed in the story\n  15 Repeating notes that build tension\n  16 Music lands on the moment\nCV-CC 2: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 6, CC 17 to 32\n   1 Sweet or clashing notes\n   2 Bent or broken music\n   3 Where the music goes\n   4 Whose feeling the music plays\n   5 Music warns us early\n   6 Music from another time\n   7 Title music\n   8 Everyday sounds turn into music\n   9 suite: Needle drop\n  10 suite: Ironic counterpoint\n  11 suite: Radio in the room\n  12 suite: Score swell\n  13 suite: Sudden silence\n  14 suite: Bare scene\n  15 suite: Suspense drone\n  16 suite: Montage song\nCV-CC 3: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 6, CC 33 to 48\n   1 suite: Returning theme\n   2 suite: Heightened sound\n   3 suite: The hero's theme returns\n   4 suite: Horror score\n   5 suite: Creepy lullaby\n   6 suite: Old story, new songs\n   7 suite: Musical number\n   8 suite: Race against the clock\n   9 suite: Spare and honest\n  10 suite: Grand opening\n  11 suite: Love theme\n  12 suite: Horror jump scare build\n  13 suite: Musical number (full style)\n  14 pair: When the music is cut dead, a big line lands\n  15 pair: When the music drops out, a reveal follows\n  16 pair: When a famous song starts, time slows\nCV-CC 4: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 6, CC 49 to 64\n   1 pair: When the tempo rises, the cuts speed up\n   2 pair: When the music turns warm, faces soften\n   3 pair: When the music fights the scene, the violence gets bigger\n   4 pair: When there is no music, the frame gets closer\n   5 pair: When music plays in the room, someone moves to it\n   6 pair: When a theme returns, the character it belongs to appears\n   7 pair: When the music builds to its peak, it cuts out\n   8 pair: When the repeating notes grow insistent, the music speeds up\n   9 pair: When the repeating notes crash to an end, the music lands on the moment\n  10 pair: When the music speeds up a lot, the cuts come faster\n  11 pair: When the music slows right down, the shots hold longer\n  12 pair: When the music turns from dark to bright, hope rises\n  13 pair: When the music turns from bright to dark, dread creeps in\n  14 pair: When the character's tune is played heroic, pride swells\n  15 pair: When a tune plays for someone who is missed, grief rises\n  16 pair: When a tune plays just before its owner arrives, the music is warning us\nCV-CC 5: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 6, CC 65 to 80\n   1 pair: When the music warns us early, dread builds\n   2 pair: When the music's warning is a false alarm, the release comes\n   3 pair: When the notes clash more, the tension rises\n   4 pair: When the clashing notes settle, the release comes\n   5 pair: When the music warps into a memory, nostalgia comes with it\n   6 pair: When the music warps, the place starts to echo\n   7 pair: When others join the humming, warmth grows\n   8 pair: When a character hums the film's own theme, the theme comes back\n   9 pair: When the crowd goes wild for a performance, pride rises\n  10 pair: When a performance takes over the scene, the music crosses into the soundtrack\n  11 pair: When room music crosses into the soundtrack, the music comes forward\n  12 pair: When the music is saved for the big moments, it lands harder\n  13 pair: When less of the film has music, the silences grow\n  14 pair: When the music plays one person's inner feeling, we feel with them\n  15 pair: When the music moves inside a character, we start to hear through their ears\n  16 pair: When the style of music clashes on purpose, the music fights the scene\nCV-CC 6: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 6, CC 81 to 96\n   1 pair: When characters sing music from another time, a performance takes over\n   2 pair: When the title music carries the main theme, the theme becomes easy to recognise\n   3 pair: When the closing music is big, the feeling stays after the film\n   4 pair: When one instrument plays alone, loneliness grows\n   5 pair: When the instrument sounds right in your ear, tenderness grows\n   6 pair: When everyday sounds fall into a beat, the cuts land on it\n   7 pair: When the music lands big on the moment, the feeling peaks\n   8 pair: When the big hit is followed by silence, the music drops out\n   9 pair: When a cheerful old song plays over cruelty, the audience feels something stranger than the scene\n  10 pair: When the danger rushes in, the music stops dead\n  11 pair: When no one speaks, the music follows every step\n  12 pair: When the big reveal lands, the orchestra swells\n  13 pair: When the hero's tune comes back, the audience lets go\n  14 pair: When the music drains away, we brace for a shock\n  15 pair: When they finally stand close, the music swells\n  16 pair: When the clock is down to seconds, the music speeds up\nCV-CC 7: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 6, CC 97 to 110\n   1 pair: When a famous song from their youth plays, the past floods back\n   2 pair: When everyday sounds fall into a beat, the song begins\n   3 pair: When the music turns out to be playing in the room, the film winks at itself\n   4 pair: When every action lands on the beat, the laughs come faster\n   5 pair: When music carries the turn from funny to sad, the tears feel earned\n   6 pairs: Music steers the edit\n   7 pairs: Silence as a weapon\n   8 pairs: The clock runs out\n   9 pairs: Something is coming\n  10 pairs: From the room to the soundtrack\n  11 pairs: The theme comes home\n  12 pairs: Saving it for the end\n  13 pairs: Horror jump scare build: the moves\n  14 pairs: Musical number: the moves"
